{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Behold, their good is not in their hand</b> — only from the Place is it given to them, even though their counsel and their words are far from me." "<b>The cords of anger He portions out to them</b> — the opposite: 'Portions have fallen to me in pleasant places' (Psalms 16:6). And some say: from the cords of a woman in labor. And the first is correct."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:03:15.669030036Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}